ment with a DOI, in the shape `literature/hartley-campbell-iodine-water` already uses in this registry; a cleared vendored source such as vendor/nasa-cea/thermo.inp is the acceptable second choice. Until a row has one of those it is supported by this paragraph and nothing else. No vendored file on this disk carries a bulk DC resistivity, so this tranche has neither of the two acceptable supports and is the weakest in the registry. Withdrawn 2026-09-13. The values themselves are physical constants of the pure elements rather than anyone's compilation, and they are quoted only to the three or four figures that a room-temperature handbook column carries; no temperature coefficient, no purity dependence and no cold-worked or alloyed value is claimed, and each row's own `notes` field states what it does not cover. Graphite is the one row that is an order of magnitude rather than a measurement, and its note says so: graphite is strongly anisotropic and its resistivity depends on the grade, so the value here describes a polycrystalline bench rod and nothing finer. Compiled 2026-09-05"],"reasons":["curated-bulk-resistivity"],"scope":"dry_solid","status":"estimated","validity":[{"lower":293.15,"quantity":"temperature","unit":"K","upper":293.15}]},{"assumptions":["Beer-Lambert additive bands; caller supplies optical path"],"observable":"absorbance","provenance":[],"reasons":["no-aqueous-sample"],"scope":"aqueous_phase","status":"unsupported","validity":[]},{"assumptions":["route coverage only, not an aggregate rate; each mechanism has progress rates in mol/L/s and its own locality, orders and catalyst inputs","absence of a selected rate model is not zero rate or inertness; equilibrium coverage does not establish kinetics"],"observable":"reaction_rate","provenance":[],"reasons":["no-selected-rate-model"],"scope":"whole_vessel","status":"unsupported","validity":[]},{"assumptions":["sealed or pressure-controlled headspace geometry; excludes liquid volume"],"observable":"headspace_volume","provenance":[],"reasons":["open-vessel-no-headspace-volume"],"scope":"whole_vessel","status":"unsupported","validity":[]},{"assumptions":["one dry sample; registry bulk density reference"],"observable":"density","provenance":[],"reasons":["curated-single-sample-density"],"scope":"dry_solid","status":"estimated","validity":[]},{"assumptions":["sum of registered nuclide activities; detector geometry and efficiency excluded"],"observable":"activity","provenance":[],"reasons":[],"scope":"whole_vessel","status":"computed","validity":[]}],"pressure_pa":101325.0,"solids":[{"colour_word":"grey","metallic":true,"moles":0.01,"name":"iron","represented_by_bulk_object":false,"settled_fraction":1.0,"species":"Fe","srgb":[120,120,125],"volume_l":0.0000709232918465837}],"temperature_k":298.15,"words":"There is grey iron in the beaker. 0% of the tracked iron is currently locked in its modeled oxide. Oxide added directly is indistinguishable from oxide formed here; this is not a corrosion rate, history, thickness, or surface coverage."}]},"step":3}
